    {
      "date": "2026-11-07",
      "text": "secdev/scapy's CONTRIBUTING requires an AI-Assisted: yes/no (tool) trailer on every commit, adapted from Wireshark's AI policy."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-11-07",
      "text": "On a slots=True dataclass, Cls.field is a slot descriptor rather than the default value. Read defaults from an instance."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-11-07",
      "text": "Scapy needs no libpcap/Npcap to read or write capture files, but building ARP() / Ether() without explicit MACs makes it resolve a local interface, which fails on Windows without Npcap. Tests set MACs explicitly."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-11-07",
      "text": "Headless Edge screenshots do not advance SMIL animation clocks reliably for SVGs in <img>; seeking with pauseAnimations() / setCurrentTime() gives exact frames."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-11-07",
      "text": "GitHub Actions runs that push to the same branch race; a concurrency group queues them."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-11-07",
      "text": "DNS labels can carry arbitrary bytes, including terminal escape sequences; tools that print query names should escape them."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-11-07",
      "text": "Hex-encoded plain text averages ~3.2\u20133.35 bits/char of Shannon entropy, random hex ~3.9 (max 4.0). A 3.5 threshold misses realistic DNS exfiltration; pcap-triage uses 3.0 plus length and unique-count conditions."
    }
